#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:402
msgid "PEP 380: Syntax for Delegating to a Subgenerator"
msgstr "PEP 380: Syntax zur Delegation an einen Untergenerator"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:404
msgid ""
"PEP 380 adds the ``yield from`` expression, allowing a :term:`generator` to "
"delegate part of its operations to another generator. This allows a section "
"of code containing :keyword:`yield` to be factored out and placed in another "
"generator. Additionally, the subgenerator is allowed to return with a value, "
"and the value is made available to the delegating generator."
msgstr ""
"PEP 380 fügt den Ausdruck ``yield from`` hinzu, mit dem ein :term:`Generator "
"<generator>` einen Teil seiner Operationen an einen anderen Generator "
"delegieren kann. So lässt sich ein Codeabschnitt mit :keyword:`yield` "
"herauslösen und in einen anderen Generator verlagern. Außerdem darf der "
"Untergenerator mit einem Wert zurückkehren, und dieser Wert steht dem "
"delegierenden Generator zur Verfügung."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:411
msgid ""
"While designed primarily for use in delegating to a subgenerator, the "
"``yield from`` expression actually allows delegation to arbitrary "
"subiterators."
msgstr ""
"Obwohl der Ausdruck ``yield from`` vor allem für die Delegation an einen "
"Untergenerator gedacht ist, erlaubt er tatsächlich die Delegation an "
"beliebige Unteriteratoren."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:414
msgid ""
"For simple iterators, ``yield from iterable`` is essentially just a "
"shortened form of ``for item in iterable: yield item``::"
msgstr ""
"Bei einfachen Iteratoren ist ``yield from iterable`` im Wesentlichen nur "
"eine Kurzform von ``for item in iterable: yield item``::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:417
msgid ""
">>> def g(x):\n"
"...     yield from range(x, 0, -1)\n"
"...     yield from range(x)\n"
"...\n"
">>> list(g(5))\n"
"[5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]"
msgstr ""
">>> def g(x):\n"
"...     yield from range(x, 0, -1)\n"
"...     yield from range(x)\n"
"...\n"
">>> list(g(5))\n"
"[5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:424
msgid ""
"However, unlike an ordinary loop, ``yield from`` allows subgenerators to "
"receive sent and thrown values directly from the calling scope, and return a "
"final value to the outer generator::"
msgstr ""
"Anders als eine gewöhnliche Schleife erlaubt ``yield from`` aber, dass "
"Untergeneratoren gesendete und geworfene Werte direkt aus dem aufrufenden "
"Gültigkeitsbereich erhalten und einen Endwert an den äußeren Generator "
"zurückgeben::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:428
msgid ""
">>> def accumulate():\n"
"...     tally = 0\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         next = yield\n"
"...         if next is None:\n"
"...             return tally\n"
"...         tally += next\n"
"...\n"
">>> def gather_tallies(tallies):\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         tally = yield from accumulate()\n"
"...         tallies.append(tally)\n"
"...\n"
">>> tallies = []\n"
">>> acc = gather_tallies(tallies)\n"
">>> next(acc)  # Ensure the accumulator is ready to accept values\n"
">>> for i in range(4):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the first tally\n"
">>> for i in range(5):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the second tally\n"
">>> tallies\n"
"[6, 10]"
msgstr ""
">>> def accumulate():\n"
"...     tally = 0\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         next = yield\n"
"...         if next is None:\n"
"...             return tally\n"
"...         tally += next\n"
"...\n"
">>> def gather_tallies(tallies):\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         tally = yield from accumulate()\n"
"...         tallies.append(tally)\n"
"...\n"
">>> tallies = []\n"
">>> acc = gather_tallies(tallies)\n"
">>> next(acc)  # Ensure the accumulator is ready to accept values\n"
">>> for i in range(4):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the first tally\n"
">>> for i in range(5):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the second tally\n"
">>> tallies\n"
"[6, 10]"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:455
msgid ""
"The main principle driving this change is to allow even generators that are "
"designed to be used with the ``send`` and ``throw`` methods to be split into "
"multiple subgenerators as easily as a single large function can be split "
"into multiple subfunctions."
msgstr ""
"Hauptgedanke dieser Änderung ist, dass sich selbst Generatoren, die zur "
"Verwendung mit den Methoden ``send`` und ``throw`` gedacht sind, so leicht "
"in mehrere Untergeneratoren aufteilen lassen, wie sich eine einzelne große "
"Funktion in mehrere Unterfunktionen aufteilen lässt."

